Fast built apps ship fast and leak often: an exposed `.env` file, SQL injection in a hand written query, a login with no rate limit, a `.git` folder served to the world. Sekudo is the MCP server you install so the model already in your editor can test your project the way an attacker would, and hand you the fixes.

It hunts hard, but only inside your fence. Recon maps the surface, the checks probe it, and every finding comes with a harmless proof and the exact place it got in. Testing systems you do not own is illegal, so the scope gate is enforced in code, not left to good intentions.
